From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:40:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: refill the receive pool when it runs dry

Only the CPU's receive refills the pool every private port shares, and
only once that CPU's count of the buffers it seeded, less those it took
out, runs low. A buffer the hardware loses leaves every count as it was,
so losses add up unseen; once the pool is empty every port discards every
frame for want of a buffer, none reaches a CPU to refill it, and nothing
is logged. Only a reboot brought receive back.

Read the pool once a second beside each port's out-of-buffer discard
count. Dry at two readings in a row, with a frame discarded since the
first, is an episode: logged once with the pool, the per-CPU counts and
the ports' counts, counted in ethtool -S, and the pool put back to what
the counts hold it to have, less the frames waiting for the CPU, within
its size, and topped up until it holds half its size. The buffers added
raise no count. An episode adds at most the pool's size, so a loss that
persists shows as repeated episodes. ethtool -S also reports BMan's free
count beside the driver's, so a deficit shows before the pool is empty.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
